# leaf37f rebuild re-verification: a comment-only source edit must not move a pixel
#
# Why this file exists. The capture batch recorded in leaf37f-fix-batch.log ran under exe
# sha256 94375d7f109f4a00e16fc8af9ecebde71f5c97120dde3f209980b2d5634a0478. After that
# batch the upload comment at native/src/native_renderer_entity.cpp was corrected (it had
# claimed ByteWidth, NumElements and the memcpy were all written from kCubeBytes; NumElements
# is in fact still capacity * kLeafAmbientFaces). Correcting a comment forces a rebuild, and
# the rebuilt exe has a different sha256 even though no code changed:
#
#   captures  94375d7f109f4a00e16fc8af9ecebde71f5c97120dde3f209980b2d5634a0478  (3434496 B)
#   rebuilt   54abaeebdc681d08cf8d6eb2bd80d7ed154bfef6b4cf321251a674b8a13a7bfd  (3434496 B)
#   source    commit b1293105, "task-37 leaf37f: six float4 rows per leaf cube, the row
#             the shader indexes" -- both builds are the same source tree
#
# Both binaries are the same size; nothing below depends on that, it is just what a rebuild
# of unchanged code gives. The point of this file is the pixel comparison underneath: every
# arm was re-captured on the rebuilt exe and every md5 is identical to the one already
# published in pins-and-counters.txt. So the pin fa297fb9... is not an artifact of one
# particular link; it is what this source produces.
#
# build: bash /d/_shared/tf2-hostlock/hostlock.sh leaf37f -- bash tools/lockrun.sh leaf37f -- \
#          bash -c 'touch native/src/native_renderer_entity.cpp && bash build-target.sh tf2_demo_native'
#        BUILD-RC=0, warning lines matching /warning/ in the build log: 0

